# Git Workflow

Solo developer hybrid workflow. Cursor agents work inline with the
developer — be more conservative than Claude Code on git operations.

## Branching decision
**Direct commit to `main`** only for trivial changes.
**Branch first** for everything else.
When uncertain — branch. Ask the developer if unsure.

## Branch naming
`feat/` `fix/` `refactor/` `chore/` `docs/` prefixes.
Kebab-case, under 40 characters.

## Commit messages — conventional commits, mandatory
Format: `<type>: <imperative subject under 72 chars>`
Types: `feat` `fix` `refactor` `chore` `docs` `test` `ci`
Imperative mood. One concept per commit.

## Always confirm with developer before
- Pushing to any remote
- Merging anything into `main`
- Creating a tag
- Deleting a branch
- Any rebase operation
- Any operation involving `--force` or `--hard`

## Never do, even with confirmation
- `git push --force` to `main`
- `git reset --hard` on `main`
- Rebase a branch already pushed
- Force-update an existing tag

## Releases
- Tag from `main` only, after merge
- Annotated tags only
- Semver strict
- Builds reference the tag, never a branch
